==English==
[[File:William Heysmann Overend Naval Captain on the Poop deck taffrail.jpg|right|thumb|''Naval Captain on the Poop Deck Taffrail'', by William Heysmann Overend]]

===Etymology===
From either {{term|tafferel|lang=en}} or {{term|aft|lang=en}} {{term|rail|lang=en}}, by false alteration.

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{context|nautical|lang=en}} The curved wooden top of the [[stern]] of a [[sailing]] [[man-of-war]] or [[East Indiaman]], usually [[carved]] or [[decorated]].
# {{context|nautical|lang=en}} The [[rail]] around the [[stern]] of a [[ship]].
# {{context|nautical|lang=en}} The [[deck]] area at the stern of a [[vessel]].

